        "body": "Intel Corporation is a public company headquartered in Santa Clara, California, traded under the ticker INTC. On its own website, Intel describes its focus as delivering AI at scale across cloud, data center, edge, and client, with hardware and software solutions, and it promotes a Googlebook built on an Intel platform covering performance, graphics, battery, and connectivity. The site also carries standard disclaimers that Intel technologies may require enabled hardware, software, or service activation, that no product or component can be absolutely secure, and that costs and results may vary.\n\nThe company's stated position is that it supplies AI capability across several computing environments rather than a single product line. Its site language centers on scale and breadth of deployment, and it pairs that with a human rights commitment, stating that Intel's products and software are intended only for applications that do not cause or contribute to adverse impacts on human rights.\n\nBeyond the site material, Intel's record includes a CIK of 0000050863 and a law exposure count of 281 in California. No products, lawsuits, or MCP servers are listed for the company.",
